.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt PIDP11-PANELTEST 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pidp11-paneltest
.Nd exercise the PiDP-11 front panel without the simulator
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl an
.Op Fl s Ar ms
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
drives the PiDP-11 front panel directly through the Raspberry Pi GPIO
header, without SIMH or the panel server.
It steps a single lit LED through all 72 LEDs (6 rows by 12 columns)
while continuously scanning the 3 x 12 switch matrix.
Whenever a switch changes state it is reported, along with the current
state of all three rows; a set bit means
.Dq switch closed .
.Pp
Switch rows 0 and 1 hold the SR switches and the ADDR/DATA select and
similar; row 2 bits 8-11 are the two rotary encoders, whose gray-code
states are shown raw.
.Pp
Only one program can hold the GPIO lines at a time, so stop the panel
server first
.Pq Cm systemctl stop pidp11-server .
.Dl Ctrl-C
releases the lines again.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl s Ar ms
Milliseconds per LED step (default 200).
.It Fl a
Light all LEDs at once instead of chasing one.
.It Fl n
No LEDs: only watch the switches.
.It Fl h
Show the usage message and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.It
The following diagnostics are printed on stderr:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It No "No Raspberry Pi GPIO header chip found"
The program is running on a machine without the Pi GPIO header, or the
libgpiod chip cannot be found.
.El
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pdp11 1
